a435-211c-5f0f-b36b-f0465eaf947a" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268699 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268699 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533957 true] [17592186268699 1111 #uuid "1198c52b-7348-59bb-aab1-0d03ff3decc0" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268700 1034 "-\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268700 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533957 true] [17592186268700 1111 #uuid "07aed2d3-b512-52c6-bf6c-75582e334af8" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268701 1034 "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268701 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533957 true] [17592186268701 1111 #uuid "567bb644-4516-5d0d-90e9-b3d724e28723" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268702 1034 "\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268702 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533957 true] [17592186268702 1111 #uuid "f56f74b2-29b7-5e0a-a001-788054524f00" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268703 1034 "\\frac{7\\pi }{4}" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268703 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533957 true] [17592186268703 1111 #uuid "fb6f4bcd-5fa7-572f-9fa0-3438e2845813" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1017 #edb/ref 17592186268705 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1089 "q-117250" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1100 "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x?$\n\n- $(1,0)$\n- $(0,\\pi )$\n- $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1113 #uuid "9985084e-755c-51fb-80a8-a70831820a0f" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268704 1145 "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [0,\\pi ].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(1,0).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(0,1)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=0$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(1,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(0,\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\pi ,0)$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,\\pi )$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x$ is $y\\in [0,\\pi ],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arccos}⁡x.$" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268706 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268707 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268708 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268709 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1000 #edb/ref 17592186268710 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1041 "selection" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1104 #edb/ref 17592186268707 13194139533957 true] [17592186268705 1110 #uuid "9016f124-6f8a-5f4d-8eae-208a665c53ce" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268706 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268706 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533957 true] [17592186268706 1111 #uuid "05d59b8c-6976-5cfb-add7-8228f1b17e50" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268707 1034 "I and III only" 13194139533957 true] [17592186268707 1103 #edb/ref 175